# Kernel config fragment — applied on top of the in-tree
# meson64_a64_smarthome_defconfig used by this build.
#
# Workaround for binutils 2.35+ (in gcc-arm-10.2-2020.11) rejecting
# R_AARCH64_ABS32 relocations against __crc_* symbols when linking the
# relocatable, position-independent vmlinux required by KASLR
# (CONFIG_RELOCATABLE=y + CONFIG_RANDOMIZE_BASE=y in the in-tree
# defconfig). The kernel community fix that uses different relocation
# types for module CRCs landed in 5.10+; since this fork pins 5.4 we
# disable MODVERSIONS instead — no module CRC version verification, but
# this is a fixed-firmware device so cross-kernel module loading is
# not a concern.
# CONFIG_MODVERSIONS is not set
